From 2fff5bf987e5bfb9b0d3f3d860f08e4c382fe6a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:16:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ft_statfun_correlationT: use n-2 degrees of freedom

The t-statistic is computed as t = r*sqrt(n-2)/sqrt(1-r^2), which has n-2
degrees of freedom, but df was set to n-1. The parametric critical value
used as the cluster-forming threshold (and the optional parametric prob)
was therefore computed with one degree of freedom too many, making the
threshold slightly too liberal: at n=8 the two-sided 0.05 critical value
was 2.365 instead of 2.447 (3.4% low). Both lines date from the same
2015 overhaul commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012d2sJAD5EUp4GqAStqoBX7
---
 statfun/ft_statfun_correlationT.m | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/statfun/ft_statfun_correlationT.m b/statfun/ft_statfun_correlationT.m
index 6d8325b..a706b34 100644
--- a/statfun/ft_statfun_correlationT.m
+++ b/statfun/ft_statfun_correlationT.m
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ if strcmp(cfg.computeprob, 'yes') && strcmp(cfg.computestat, 'no')
 end
 
 [nsmpl, nrepl] = size(dat);
-df = nrepl - 1;
+df = nrepl - 2;
 if df<1
   ft_error('Insufficient degrees of freedom for this analysis.')
 end
